# Architecture Decision Records

This repo is **one project** (EduConsult CRM, built via an agent-harnessed
delivery process). Its single canonical ADR log lives at `docs/adr/`
(index: `docs/adr/README.md`, template: `docs/adr/TEMPLATE.md`).
`harness-demo/adr/` is a frozen historical log (see `docs/adr/0008`) —
never add new entries there.

## When to write or update an ADR

Whenever you (the agent) make, or the user directs, a decision that is
**significant and hard to reverse** — e.g. tech stack, data model /
multi-tenancy approach, auth/security model, deployment topology, agent
architecture, CI/CD or test-gating policy, major API/schema conventions —
record it as an ADR. Skip ADRs for routine implementation details, bug
fixes, or anything easily reversed in a single PR.

## How

1. **New decision**: add `docs/adr/NNNN-kebab-title.md` (next sequential
   number) using `docs/adr/TEMPLATE.md`'s structure (Status, Date, Context,
   Decision, Alternatives considered, Consequences). Add a row to the
   index table in `docs/adr/README.md`.
2. **Decision changes or is reversed**: do **not** edit the old ADR's
   Context/Decision text. Write a **new** ADR describing the new decision,
   then update the old ADR's `**Status**:` line to
   `Superseded by ADR-NNNN` (linking the new one), and update both rows in
   the index table.
3. Do this proactively, in the same turn as the decision is made — don't
   wait to be asked. If you're unsure whether something rises to
   "significant," err toward writing a short ADR rather than skipping it.
